---
/**
 * Primary money page — targets "yacht management Newport Beach".
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Placeholder from '../components/Placeholder.astro';
import { url } from '../config';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'What is the difference between yacht management and calling a mechanic when something breaks?',
    a: 'A mechanic fixes what has already failed. Yacht management holds the whole schedule — every system, every due date, every vendor — so most of the work is planned rather than reactive, and so there is one continuous record of what was done to the vessel.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you require us to use your vendors?',
    a: 'No. If you have a mechanic or a yard you already trust, we schedule and coordinate them. Our job is that the work happens on time and is documented, not that it is done by any particular shop.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you work on vessels at private residential docks?',
    a: 'Yes. Much of Newport Harbor is residential dockage — Balboa Island, Lido Isle, Linda Isle, Bayshores — and we service vessels at private docks as well as in slips and on moorings.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Yacht Management in Newport Beach"
  description="Yacht management in Newport Beach for owners who want the boat ready and the answers on hand. Scheduled maintenance, managed vendors, documented work."
  path="/yacht-management-newport-beach"
  heading="Yacht management in Newport Beach"
  kind="service"
  faq={faq}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Newport Beach, California</p>
      <h1>Yacht management in Newport Beach.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        We hold the maintenance schedule, run the vendors, keep the compliance
        paperwork current, and give you a live view of all of it. You bought the
        boat to use it.
      </p>
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href={url('/contact')}>Request a Consultation</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why it compounds here</p>
      <h2>Newport Harbor is a demanding place to keep a boat.</h2>
      <p>
        Newport Harbor is one of the largest recreational harbors on the West
        Coast, and it is a working saltwater environment. Growth on the running
        gear, corrosion on underwater metals, sun load on canvas and brightwork,
        and the usage rate of a Southern California season all accumulate faster
        than most owners expect.
      </p>
      <p>
        None of that is unusual. What makes it expensive is letting it accumulate
        unnoticed until the boat is unavailable the weekend you wanted it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Scope</p>
      <h2>What we take off your plate.</h2>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>
          A complete systems inventory — engines, generator, watermaker, HVAC,
          electronics, hull and running gear — with serial numbers, engine hours
          and warranty windows recorded
        </li>
        <li>A maintenance schedule generated from that inventory, tracked by both calendar time and engine hours</li>
        <li>Lead-time alerting so haul-outs, bottom work, engine services and survey deadlines surface before they come due</li>
        <li>Vendor scheduling, attendance and verification of completed work</li>
        <li>Registration, documentation and insurance-survey deadline tracking</li>
        <li>Cost capture against each job, rolled into a single monthly statement</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Getting started</p>
      <h2>The first visit is an inventory, not a sales call.</h2>
      <p>
        We walk the vessel, record every major system with its serial number and
        hours, note current condition, and collect the service records and
        documentation you already have. That becomes the baseline — from it we
        build the schedule, identify anything already overdue, and give you a
        written picture of where the vessel actually stands.
      </p>
      <div class="notice">
        <p>
          <strong>Initial inventory visit:</strong>
          <Placeholder
            key="onboardTiming"
            label="whether the initial inventory visit is complimentary or billed, and at what rate — CEO to confirm"
          />
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Cost</p>
      <h2>What it costs.</h2>
      <div class="notice">
        <p>
          <strong>Management fee structure:</strong>
          <Placeholder
            key="pricing"
            label="pricing model — flat monthly by vessel length, tiered, or percentage of spend. Nothing about pricing is published until the CEO supplies this"
          />
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        What we can commit to now: vendor invoices are passed through at cost and
        shown to you individually, and the management fee is stated separately.
        You will not receive a single opaque number.
      </p>
      <div class="notice">
        <p>
          <strong>Vessel size range:</strong>
          <Placeholder key="terms" label="the vessel size range we take on — CEO to confirm" />
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Common questions.</h2>
      {
        faq.map((item) => (
          <div class="qa">
            <h3>{item.q}</h3>
            <p>{item.a}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
      <div class="notice">
        <p>
          <strong>After-hours and emergency coverage:</strong>
          <Placeholder
            key="responseTime"
            label="emergency and after-hours coverage — CEO to confirm. Do not state a response time we have not staffed for"
          />
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Where we work.</h2>
      <p>
        We serve vessels throughout Newport Harbor, including private docks on
        <a href={url('/boat-management-balboa-island')}>Balboa Island</a> and
        <a href={url('/boat-management-lido-isle')}>Lido Isle</a>, slips along the
        Balboa Peninsula, and moorings in the main channel. See also
        <a href={url('/yacht-maintenance-newport-harbor')}>yacht maintenance in Newport Harbor</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
